    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99c775a6_38c3bcce",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-15T20:51:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Soong APIs used for exposing jar files from java_import to its consumers (e.g. java_library) do not allow for error reporting (other than panic) if the requested file is not available. All that they can do is return nil which is usually ignored. So, the only error that it will get is a compilation error because of missing classes which is completely unhelpful.\n\nModifying that API to support providing meaningful errors is a reasonably large amount of work that would have delayed this by at least a week if not more.\n\nReturning an empty and invalid jar with a weird name gives a slightly more helpful message and doesn\u0027t require any modifications to java_import.",
      "parentUuid": "cd059f7b_5627ebf0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 96
      },
      "revId": "ddcd4b77c574413844a641ba299da94d63121401",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8aa82cbc_d7022c95",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-15T00:37:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a bit of a hacky way to create an empty file, and I\u0027m somewhat wary of using absolute paths. Suggestion: change this to return an OptionalPath, and add something like SnapshotBuilder.CreateEmptyInSnapshot that uses android.Touch to create the file.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "ddcd4b77c574413844a641ba299da94d63121401",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "668e58ff_97c85018",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-15T20:51:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The value returned from this function is ignored if it is nil. So, we need to differentiate between three cases:\n1. Ignore the file.\n2. An empty file to be copied.\n3. A real file to be copied.\n\nAn OptionalPath provides no advantage over returning nil. We would still need to differentiate between 2 and 3.\n\nWe could make the return value a pair of (Path, bool) but using /dev/null just seemed less disruptive. My main concern with using that was whether it would work well with ninja.\n\nAlternatively, I did consider creating an empty file that could be used for copying from but there did not seem a good place to do that.",
      "parentUuid": "8aa82cbc_d7022c95",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "ddcd4b77c574413844a641ba299da94d63121401",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
